      "urpx:forRatePlan": {
        "@id": "gpc:aps"
      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "gpc:cc-aps-2026-06-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "gpc:cc-aps-2026-06-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 6 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Fuel and demand seasons by billing month. FCR-27 prices June through September and October through May, which Schedule R's bills show is read by the billing month a bill is rendered in, and APS-18 prices its Demand Charge by Summer (June through September) and Winter (October through May), with an alternative rate \"for bills rendered October - May\". The JSON-LD gates the fuel and Demand Charge PriceDefinitions on calendar months, so usage in the weeks a billing period runs ahead of its billing month takes the other season's prices. (2) Voltage level and franchise fee location. FCR-27's three voltage levels and MFF-11's two locations are crossed in one ProfileAlternatives set of six alternatives, because URPX v0.5.1 allows one set per PlanElements and the franchise fee's energy subtotal must include that voltage level's fuel prices. A consumer selects one alternative, for example Secondary Distribution inside city limits. (3) Municipal Franchise Fee base. MFF-11 applies to the total revenues of each bill, which include the ECCR-15 and DSM-C-15 amounts. Its multiplier Prices here are based on the energy-and-fuel subtotal and on the non-energy charges' Prices, not on the ECCR and DSM-C multiplier Prices, so the franchise fee on those two amounts, about 0.44 percent of the base bill inside city limits, is not carried. (4) Alternative Monthly Rate. For bills rendered October through May, the bill is the lesser of the bill calculated above or 16.5579 cents per kWh plus the $43.72 Basic Service Charge. A lesser-of is a choice between two bills, which no Price expresses, so it is not carried; a modeled winter bill above the alternative is high by the difference. (5) Minimum Monthly Bill. The sheet sets it at the $43.72 Basic Service Charge plus ECCR, DSM and the Municipal Franchise Fee, and no Price carries it. Every price here is positive, so a bill on these prices alone is never below it. (6) Term of Contract. Five years. Nothing is priced by it and it is not carried.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-19T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
